      "section": "Differential expression",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One row per gene from a differential expression test, read three ways with the switch in the tile header: volcano (fold change against significance), MA (fold change against mean abundance, where low-count noise shows as a funnel) and QQ (observed against expected p-values, where a curve lifting off early means an inflated test). The input is a DESeq2 or limma results table as nf-core/differentialabundance publishes it after nf-core/rnaseq.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
